            The math is simple. Multiply the package weight by the protein percentage to get the total protein, divide the price by that total, and multiply by 25. For the Swiss Miss tub, 1,288 g at 35.1 percent gives about 452 g of protein; $12.13 divided by 452 and multiplied by 25 is about $0.67. For hemp hearts, 2,268 g at a labeled 10 g per 30 g gives about 756 g of protein, or about $1.42 per 25 g. Small packs cost far more: the 16 oz Manitoba Harvest bag at $11.67 works out near $1.93 per 25 g.
